RESOLVED 2026-08-17: Nuked-OPL3 is now vendored here.

  opl3.c / opl3.h   Copyright (C) 2013-2020 Nuke.YKT, LGPL-2.1, unmodified
  LICENSE           the full LGPL-2.1 text as shipped upstream

The shim is src/music_opl_nuked.c and opl_core_is_real() returns 1. The stub
below is kept for reference and for measuring without a chip.

Everything from here down is the note the previous session left.
--------------------------------------------------------------------

THIS DIRECTORY WAS EMPTY ON PURPOSE, AND THAT WAS A KNOWN GAP.

Phase 8 (music) needs an OPL2 / YM3812 emulation. Writing one is a mistake -
it is a solved problem with two good, permissively licensed implementations -
so the plan was to vendor one. That did not happen in the session that wrote
the sequencer: the machine had no local copy (dosbox-x and dosbox-staging are
installed as binaries only, no sources), and fetching one from the network was
outside what that session was allowed to do.

What is compiled in instead is src/music_opl_stub.c. Read its header. It is a
tone probe used to MEASURE pitch and timing; it is not a synthesiser and the
output is not the game's sound.

TO FIX IT
---------

Pick one:

  Nuked-OPL3   https://github.com/nukeykt/Nuked-OPL3
               files: opl3.c, opl3.h        licence: LGPL-2.1
               cycle-exact, the reference these days.
               API:  OPL3_Reset(&chip, rate)
                     OPL3_WriteRegBuffered(&chip, reg, val)
                     OPL3_GenerateStream(&chip, int16 *buf, num)   [stereo]
               OPL2 is reached by only ever writing the low register bank
               (0x00..0xF5) and leaving the OPL3 "new" bit (reg 0x105) clear,
               which is exactly what our driver layer does.

  ymfm         https://github.com/aaronsgiles/ymfm
               files: src/ymfm_opl.{cpp,h} + ymfm.h + ymfm_fm.* ...
               licence: BSD-3-Clause. C++; needs a small extern "C" shim.

Then:

  1. Drop the sources in here, LICENCE file included, unmodified.
  2. Add src/music_opl_nuked.c (about 40 lines) implementing the five
     functions in src/music_opl.h on top of the core:
         opl_reset / opl_write / opl_render / opl_core_name / opl_core_is_real
     opl_render() must down-mix to mono (the four drivers Stunts shipped are
     all mono) and resample 49716 Hz -> host rate; Nuked can generate
     directly at the host rate with OPL3_GenerateResampled, which is simpler
     and is what you want.
     Keep opl_write_hook working - music_native_dump_opl() depends on it.
  3. Swap music_opl_stub.c for it in tools/build_native.sh and
     tools/build_music_tool.sh.
  4. Make opl_core_is_real() return 1. music_native_opl_is_real() is what
     anything claiming "the music sounds right" is supposed to check.

VERIFICATION AFTER SWAPPING
---------------------------

Nothing about the sequencer changes, so all the numbers in
docs/FAITHFUL_RENDERER.md "Phase 8" must be reproduced exactly:

    ./bin/music_tool --dump-events title      # byte-identical to before
    ./bin/music_tool --dump-opl title 4.0     # byte-identical to before

Only the .wav changes. Then re-run the pitch measurement:

    ./bin/music_tool --wav title 12 /tmp/t.wav
    python3 tools/analyse_music_wav.py /tmp/t.wav
